; A segment's cards, again for each of its frames. First a card saying how many cards a segment has besides its
; frames n, w (at most 20); then for each segment n and those w cards. Out, for each of its n frames, the w cards
; again, so that the machines that work frame by frame read each frame's segment beside it. The cards are kept in
; cells 70 onwards; the INP and OUT that reach them are moved on a cell for each card.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03                    INP   w        03-05: w, and the instructions' ends
  04                    CLA   i70
  05                    ADD   w
  06                    STO   iend
  07                    CLA   o70
  08                    ADD   w
  09                    STO   oend
  10            seg     INP   n        10-22: a segment: its cards
  11                    CLA   i70
  12                    STO   rd
  13            rd      DATA  0        (INP 70 + k)
  14                    CLA   rd
  15                    ADD   00
  16                    STO   rd
  17                    SUB   iend
  18                    TAC   rd
  19            frm     CLA   n        19-34: each frame: the cards again
  20                    SUB   00
  21                    TAC   seg
  22                    STO   n
  23                    CLA   o70
  24                    STO   wr
  25            wr      DATA  0        (OUT 70 + k)
  26                    CLA   wr
  27                    ADD   00
  28                    STO   wr
  29                    SUB   oend
  30                    TAC   wr
  31                    JMP   frm
  40            w       DATA  0
  41            n       DATA  0
  42            iend    DATA  0
  43            oend    DATA  0
  44            i70     INP   70
  45            o70     OUT   70
